WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:07.665
AEGIS puts an inspectable control boundary around AI requests. This example is
a company policy assistant, built

2
00:00:07.665 --> 00:00:14.503
to show how developers can handle access, privacy, suspicious input, and
request evidence in one gateway.

3
00:00:15.703 --> 00:00:22.794
A website or workflow sends requests through its own backend to AEGIS. The
gateway checks the tenant, screens

4
00:00:22.794 --> 00:00:28.704
supported attack patterns, masks recognized personal data, and calls a
configured provider. Keep credentials on

5
00:00:28.704 --> 00:00:29.492
the server.

6
00:00:30.703 --> 00:00:37.381
Open the console and choose Vacation days. The request retrieves fictional
company policies. Inspect the source

7
00:00:37.381 --> 00:00:44.478
and provider label beside the response. This public demo uses echo, which
returns deterministic test output. It

8
00:00:44.478 --> 00:00:47.400
does not generate an intelligent policy answer.

9
00:00:48.603 --> 00:00:55.260
Choose Try privacy check, then expand Show details for the newest response.
The original message contains a

10
00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:01.525
fictional email. In the outbound provider payload, that value becomes an
alias. AEGIS restores recognized values

11
00:01:01.525 --> 00:01:05.441
for the caller. Detection is pattern based and has limits.

12
00:01:06.641 --> 00:01:13.143
Choose Try attack attempt. The gateway refuses this supported suspicious
request. Inspect the decision and

13
00:01:13.143 --> 00:01:18.777
absent outbound payload. The recorded engineering experiment separately checks
that the recording provider

14
00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:24.412
received zero additional calls. This is a specific test, not universal attack
protection.

15
00:01:25.612 --> 00:01:32.339
The engineering showcase labels its results as a recorded run. It demonstrates
poisoned retrieved context,

16
00:01:32.339 --> 00:01:38.618
tenant-state separation, an injected provider failure, and an altered audit-
copy record that fails verification.

17
00:01:38.618 --> 00:01:43.103
Reproduce these experiments with the evidence command in the repository.

18
00:01:44.312 --> 00:01:52.248
Your backend can call the chat API with a scoped tenant key. A document
assistant uses the ingestion and

19
00:01:52.248 --> 00:01:58.095
retrieval endpoints instead of plain chat. Handle refusals, usage limits,
unavailable providers, and echo

20
00:01:58.095 --> 00:02:01.436
fallback explicitly. Native company connectors are not included.

21
00:02:02.646 --> 00:02:10.907
Start with the public showcase, explore the source, and reproduce the checks.
AEGIS is a working gateway

22
00:02:10.907 --> 00:02:17.224
prototype for a controlled integration pilot. Real-model quality, approved
company data, persistence, and

23
00:02:17.224 --> 00:02:20.139
operational acceptance still require deployment-specific verification.
